WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.783
The fulfillment by Amazon FBA dashboard provides a summarized view of your FBA sales, shipments,

00:00:08.783 --> 00:00:10.540
inventory, and opportunities.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:18.120
To locate the FBA dashboard, open the Seller Central main menu, hover over Inventory and click Dashboard.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.661
On the main page of the FBA dashboard, you'll see the first section contains your key performance

00:00:24.661 --> 00:00:25.020
indicators.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:32.387
These four cards, Sales Ordered, Units Ordered, Orders, and FBA Fees, summarize your sales and show

00:00:32.387 --> 00:00:37.040
a year-over-year comparison as well as any incurred fees.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.980
You can also filter these metrics by date.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.000
Click the arrow above the Sales Ordered card for the drop-down menu to appear.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.860
Then choose a date range or set a customized range by selecting Custom.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:57.044
In the Plan Inventory card below your key performance indicators, you'll find the Inventory Performance

00:00:57.044 --> 00:00:58.960
Index or IPI score.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:03.920
This score is based on how well you drive sales and manage on-hand inventory.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:11.090
It's important to keep an eye on your IPI score as falling below the threshold may limit your storage

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:11.440
volume.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.620
If you click View Details, you'll be directed to the IPI page.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:22.338
Also, in the Plan Inventory card, top-influencing factors is shown on the right and highlights actions

00:01:22.338 --> 00:01:25.500
you can take to improve your IPI score.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.980
Hover over each link to learn more.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.320
The Shipments card provides data about your shipment statuses over the past 120 days.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:41.084
It breaks down your shipments into four categories, Working Shipments, In Transit Shipments, At

00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:43.720
Fulfillment Center, and Closed Shipments.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:49.012
If you want to see more detail, click View All Shipments and you'll be directed to the Shipping

00:01:49.012 --> 00:01:49.600
Queue page.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:55.160
Shipment problems, such as shipments missing their tracking IDs, are also flagged here.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:01.940
The Estimated Aged Inventory surcharge card helps you prevent Aged inventory surcharge fees.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.920
It shows you how many units of your inventory are within a certain age range.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.704
This helps you clearly see how many units are in danger of going over the threshold

00:02:12.704 --> 00:02:15.200
and incurring an aged inventory surcharge fee.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:22.977
Finally, the Optimize Inventory card shows you SKUs that we recommend you restock due to low supply

00:02:22.977 --> 00:02:25.560
or manage due to excess inventory.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:32.496
You'll also see what products qualify for recommended actions, such as creating an outlet deal,

00:02:32.496 --> 00:02:37.120
creating a removal order, advertising a listing, and restocking inventory.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:44.157
Click the link to navigate to a filtered view of the FBA Inventory page where you'll find the specific

00:02:44.157 --> 00:02:45.180
SKUs to optimize.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.920
At the top of the page, you can find the FBA Navigation menu.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:58.332
The Inventory menu has links to manage and optimize your FBA inventory with tools for planning demand,

00:02:58.332 --> 00:02:59.258
monitoring performance,

00:02:59.258 --> 00:03:02.500
and updating your product and inventory listings.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:09.533
The next menu, Shipments, has links to help you manage the delivery of your inventory and understand

00:03:09.533 --> 00:03:10.360
shipping performance.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:17.680
On the Opportunities page, we analyze your catalog and recommend which ASINs to enroll in FBA.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:23.996
You can switch between viewing only recommended products for FBA enrollment or view all the products

00:03:23.996 --> 00:03:25.180
from your catalog.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:30.180
The last menu option, Analytics, helps you visualize your sales data.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:37.503
You can select from three different tabs to help you analyze sales trends, filter by date and SKU

00:03:37.503 --> 00:03:38.630
for performance metrics,

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.260
and gain insights to top-selling SKUs.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:47.767
If you need more information, visit the FBA Dashboard Help page for a variety of links that will

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:51.020
guide you through your most critical inventory management pages.
